I stopped working on the ms as I when trying to explain how the landscape types plays out in the regression tree. When looking at the code producing the results table from Jonatan "ResultsWithoutMortality_new_mod.csv" (in Dropbox/TillAnna/Regression/LongInitNoMortality) it seems like the landscape types are calculated on a single landscape, not two equal ones put together. Code for defining landscape types 6A, 6B and 6C is in "extractResults.m".\
\
I have written some code for working on the conversion of empirical landscapes to point pattern and then compare them. \
\
\
extractLandscape_new.R  - script for extracting simulated landscapes from .mat result files\
\
toPPP.R - script for making a point pattern from the empirical raster dat\
\
